{
  // Biome check (the 3x3 climate grid of BIOMEGEN.md): run from OpenGLTest/ with
  //   VOXEL_TIME=147 VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/biomes.json
  // Shots land in visual/biomes/. VOXEL_TIME=147 is noon, so the grass tint is read under a high,
  // neutral sun: steppe and savanna grass should read drier and yellower than the forest's, no
  // strip of forest should stand between sand and snow, and the climate's domain warp
  // (TerrainNoise.ClimateWarp) should bend the biome borders instead of tracing smooth blobs.
  //
  // The vantage points come from a headless probe over TerrainGenerator.BiomeAt, BiomeWeights,
  // ColumnCache.Get, SnowGenerator.DepthAt, TreeGenerator.TryGetTree and
  // CottonGenerator.TryGetCotton, FoliageGenerator.TryGetDeadShrub and the columns' DirtDepth
  // (default seed, warped climate):
  //   forest         - all forest within 96 blocks of (-64, -112), ground 11-17; the camera
  //                    looks north into it
  //   steppe         - all steppe within 96 blocks of (16, 144), ground up to about 11 with a few
  //                    low wet spots; the camera looks west, away from the desert line to the east
  //   steppe_desert  - steppe at (96, 16) with the desert about 90 blocks to the south-east
  //   savanna_desert - savanna at (192, -48) with the desert about 64 blocks to the south and
  //                    steppe to the west
  //   savanna        - all savanna within 48 blocks of (1392, -1216), ground 14-17, with stone
  //                    pines (the acacia stand-in, e.g. (1365, 15, -1212)) and cotton clumps
  //   desert         - all desert within 96 blocks of (576, 1184), ground 7-19, with cacti
  //   steppe_tundra  - steppe at (-480, 1056) with frozen tundra about 70 blocks west-south-west
  //   ragged_border  - the desert/savanna line through (576, 1696), (608, 1728) and (640, 1760),
  //                    filmed from height looking along it (north-east), so the warp's bends show
  //                    as the sand edge wanders across the frame
  //   tundra         - a flat frozen plain around (-764, 1348), ground 11-13, filmed from low
  //                    height looking north (+Z): dead_tree snags (e.g. (-764, 12, 1336)) and sparse
  //                    dead shrubs poke out of a 4-5 layer snow cover over permafrost
  //   tundra_permafrost - a frozen ravine running north-east through (-1110, 816) (floor -9, bed
  //                    16), filmed from its south rim (ground 15 at z 806) looking north (+Z)
  //                    across it at its north wall (rim 17 at z 824, soil 2-4): the permafrost band
  //                    shows between the snow on the rim and the bare stone of the stripped ravine
  //                    wall below. (The ravine at (-888, -138) this shot used was cut into a
  //                    mountain the relief layer removed: ranges now rise only inside highlands.)
  //   pack_ice       - the pack-ice edge of a cold sea, from the open water at (-952, -2536), 120
  //                    blocks up, looking up the cold gradient (north-west, toward -X and +Z) at the
  //                    band centered near (-1090, -2440): open leads and loose floes thicken into the
  //                    solid, snow-covered sheet past the freeze line (SnowGenerator.IsFrozenWater)
  //   pack_ice_low   - a grazing shot just above an open lead at (-1056, -2456), inside the band,
  //                    looking the same way across the floes to the sheet behind them
  //                    (since phase C's islands (BIOMEGEN 13.2) a wooded island rises out of the sea
  //                    just south-west of the band, around (-1100, -2510), and small islands stand
  //                    in the sheet beyond; pack_ice shows the first in the foreground. The open
  //                    leads, the floes and the sheet still read, so the shots stay where they are)
  // The camera flies (so it hovers instead of falling), every teleport is followed by a wait while
  // the streaming ring fills around the new position, and the repeat teleport restores the exact
  // pose before the frame is taken.
  "steps": [
    { "op": "fly" },

